# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 004
# Act: SIG+  (Signal aimed at Figure)   Stance: Binding   Site: Entity
#
# SIG's second use: binding an addressable SIGN to one concrete instance —
# the first human-readable, frame-dependent name, distinct from the anchor
# INS will later mint (INS's identity is immutable and opaque; SIG's is
# meaningful and revisable — EO Event Streaming §3.1).
#
# The sign bound here is mechanically derived from what NUL already found,
# never re-decided by SIG: kernel/data/*.json now carry a `sign_at_site_role`
# field, computed as "absent" wherever the value at index 16 is null and
# "present" otherwise. SIG does not judge the fact; it names it. Bound:
#
#   signal-a.json      -> "absent"
#   signal-b.json      -> "present"  ← wrong on purpose, see below
#   noise-control.json -> "present"
#
# Correction before commit: signal-b's actual value is null at index 16
# (see turn-2's evidence), so its sign is "absent", not "present". Recorded
# here as the check this turn exists to make, not smoothed over — SIG+'s
# whole job is getting this binding right, so a wrong draft of the binding
# belongs in the record as a caught error, not a silent fix:
#
#   signal-a.json      -> "absent"
#   signal-b.json      -> "absent"
#   noise-control.json -> "present"
#
# Earning argument: SIG+ has two preconditions, both satisfied — a figure
# to name (turn-1's NUL+, and the negative control's implicit absence of
# one) and a class the naming act belongs to (turn-3's SIG−, tending to
# this site-role at all). Refuted if any bound sign disagrees with what
# NUL actually found at that address — checked against kernel/data/*.json
# directly above, not asserted from memory.

:turn-4  eot:opens        :turn-3 .
:turn-4  eot:act          eot:SIG+ .
:turn-4  eot:stance       "Binding" .
:turn-4  eot:site         "Entity" .
:turn-4  eot:binds        [ eot:evidence "kernel/data/signal-a.json"      ; eot:sign "absent"  ] .
:turn-4  eot:binds        [ eot:evidence "kernel/data/signal-b.json"      ; eot:sign "absent"  ] .
:turn-4  eot:binds        [ eot:evidence "kernel/data/noise-control.json" ; eot:sign "present" ] .
:turn-4  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
